Z||000017||jlhuber||01-14-2001||01:33 AM||||You got me thinkin' here.  Ever since I drove a handful of Syclones, I want to make everything I drive an AWD.  An AWD Fiero, what do you think?  Take a Syclone motor and drive system and *slightly* modify it to fit in a Fiero.  Granted that the Corvette 700R4 tranny that is used in a Syclone would never fit in a Fiero unless you had the front engine option, but who said the 700R4 would have to be used.  All you need is the front drive axle and transfercase which can be found on GMC's: Syclone, Typhoon, Safari, and Olds Bravada, use a 'vette rearend to retain the 4-wheel independent suspension.  Actually, now that I think about it, if you left the engine in a transverse setup, how would you drive the front axle?  Wait a muinute, the Lambo's are AWD now and they use a longitude rear mounted engine.  We could use a setup like they use.  Someone on this forum (Hugh? maybe) did the longitudal engine in a Fiero.  Anyone had a close-up look at a new Lamborghini?  I'd bet that with enough money and time, it could be made to work.  Eh, maybe I ought to just qiut dreaming huh?    ||||reg||3
Z||000018||Standard||01-14-2001||08:38 AM||||I was thinking about an all-wheel drive setup in one of my dreaming phases... relocate the gas tank and you have more than enough room to run a driveshaft through there.  The tough part would be figuring out what you could use... anything is possible with money||||reg||
